+_Datagram_SlistPing -- vkquake-ios R6.3
+
+The round trip, in milliseconds, for a reply that has just arrived from `addr`.
+
+Two clocks, because there are two kinds of query. An internet search unicasts a
+query per host (from hostlist[], max four per 100 ms poll) so each host has its own
+send time and the RTT is exact. A LAN search only ever broadcasts, so no per-host
+record exists and the broadcast time is the only honest reference — on a LAN that
+is sub-millisecond anyway.
